Package: forestPulse
Type: Package
Title: Analyse Forest Structure and Disturbance from Field and Remote Sensing Data
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Sushil", family = "Paudel", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "clarkesushi@gmail.com")
Description: Analyse forest structure and disturbance dynamics from field
    measurements and remote-sensing imagery, and assemble inputs for forest
    landscape simulation. Functions index geotagged rasters into a spatial
    catalog matched to field plots, compute canopy height models and canopy
    gap geometry, derive RGB vegetation indices, locate trees from compass
    bearings, and summarise plot-level basal area, crown density, and species
    composition. Further tools impute field plots to pixels to build
    wall-to-wall tree lists, derive daily climate variables such as vapour
    pressure deficit and radiation from 'gridMET' data, and build stand
    grids, resource-unit environment files, tree-initialisation files, and
    'SQLite' climate databases for the 'iLand' forest landscape model.
